{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"accused-disyllabic-bovine","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` Step 7, Axis 1 \"Class review\" item 1 (introduced by story dff2-9c38-c454-4daa) **unconditionally** mandates that every confirmed sibling class add \"one criterion asserting a structural check over the class (a construct-uniqueness guard, or an equivalent that fails if a new instance appears)\". Mandating a structural guard for *every* class that has ≥1 sibling over-produces guards: it invites CI bloat, standing maintenance burden, and change-detector checks for classes whose re-entry risk a plain regression test already covers. The skill has no guidance for *when* a guard is warranted or *how* to design a non-brittle, portable one.\n\nThis follow-on (requested by the operator this session) converts that unconditional mandate into a **bright-line evaluation**, backed by a new conditionally-loaded companion prompt, `structural-guards.md`, mirroring how `test-design.md` and `llm-behavioral-taxonomy.md` are loaded on demand.\n\n## Scope (documentation only — no code, no ticket-system change)\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/structural-guards.md` (NEW) — the companion prompt: a default-off framing (the RED→GREEN regression test is the guard for a single-site bug), five affirmative bright-line \"does this class earn a guard?\" questions, proportionate fallbacks when it does not, a portability table mapping bug shape → guard shape across stacks (type-system exhaustiveness / architecture-import rule / custom AST lint / consumer contract / derived-invariant + liveness floor), five design properties of a non-brittle guard, a proof step reusing the mutation artifact, and in-repo exemplars (the deploy-manifest derive-and-diff guard; the repo-root construct guard).\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` — Step 7 Axis-1 item 1 flips from the unconditional guard mandate to \"decide via structural-guards.md; add the criterion when the test says yes, else record the one-line reason and rely on per-sibling regression tests.\"\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Step 7 item 1 no longer unconditionally mandates a structural check; it routes the decision through `structural-guards.md` and preserves the per-sibling acceptance-criterion requirement.\n- [ ] `structural-guards.md` exists, states what it governs and when each skill loads it, and gives affirmative bright-line WHEN questions and non-brittle HOW-to-design properties, portable across tech stacks.\n- [ ] The guidance is affirmative-framed (describes good-guard properties rather than priming with anti-patterns).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py` stays green (the Step-7 directive's semantic contract — review-plan, set-file-impact, acceptance criteria, Phase-1 cross-ref, blast-radius non-duplication, tracker portability — is preserved).\n- [ ] `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py`, `scripts/check_docs_index.py`, and `tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py` stay green (the new companion needs no frontmatter and is not a shared-synced file).\n\n## Test plan\n\nDocumentation change: `make lint` (ruff over Python is unaffected) plus the three skill contract tests above. No runtime behavior changes.\n\n## Attribution\n\nThis is an additive skill enhancement, not a defect fix — it evolves the Step-7 directive that story dff2-9c38-c454-4daa shipped. Relates-to dff2 and its epic e71b (bug-trend program: debug-skill upgrades).","id":"71b5-1ceb-131a-422d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["rebar-debug","skill","structural-guards"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"rebar-debug Step 7: gate the class structural-guard on an evaluation, add structural-guards.md companion"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788132711016040431,"uuid":"374a8a11-ab39-4d16-b107-779d6f5ae2fb"}